@startuml
title stm — BenchController lifecycle
[*] --> Stopped
Stopped --> Running : start / initialization succeeds
Stopped --> Fault : start / initialization fails
state Running {
  [*] --> Waiting
  Waiting --> Pending : due / single-shot accepted
  Pending --> Waiting : TX_SUCCESS without fault
}
Running --> Fault : submission failure, TX_FAILED, timeout or bus-off
Running --> Stopped : stop or USB loss / cleanup succeeds
Running --> Fault : stop or USB loss / cleanup fails
Fault --> Stopped : stop / cleanup succeeds and no bus-off latch
Stopped --> Stopped : stop, status, help or invalid command
note right of Running
Repeated start does not reset cadence.
status/help do not transmit.
Invalid commands are rejected.
Faults take priority over success.
end note
note right of Fault
No automatic retry.
Bus-off requires device reset.
Every reset returns to Stopped.
start is rejected in Fault.
Cleanup failure remains Fault.
end note
@enduml
